From c5a9df03b2096646bf8e8786a8d614b3e32b3c23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 01:39:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Do not touch a node panel that was never created

updatePosition indexed nodes[nodeNum] and dereferenced the result straight
away. nodes is an unordered_map, so operator[] inserts a null panel for a key
it does not hold - and the next line writes through it.

That happens in normal operation: the node list is bounded and untracked
senders are logged as "not in db and no need to insert", yet their positions
still reach here. On a busy mesh it panicked with StoreProhibited about once a
minute, always immediately after a burst of POSITION_APP packets, taking the
reboot count from 198 to 267 in one afternoon.

Guarded at the top of the function rather than at the crashing line, because
everything below assumes the panel exists - several later statements index
nodes[] the same way.

The same operator[]-then-dereference shape appears at roughly two dozen other
call sites in this file. They are left alone here: this is the one that fires,
and changing all of them is a separate, much larger piece of work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjqMrWWLWXvmh69rvGCEo
---
 source/graphics/TFT/TFTView_320x240.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/graphics/TFT/TFTView_320x240.cpp b/source/graphics/TFT/TFTView_320x240.cpp
index 3005bac..e681316 100644
--- a/source/graphics/TFT/TFTView_320x240.cpp
+++ b/source/graphics/TFT/TFTView_320x240.cpp
@@ -4945,6 +4945,18 @@ void TFTView_320x240::updateNode(uint32_t nodeNum, uint8_t ch, const meshtastic_
 
 void TFTView_320x240::updatePosition(uint32_t nodeNum, int32_t lat, int32_t lon, int32_t alt, uint32_t sats, uint32_t precision)
 {
+    // A position can arrive from a node this view never built a panel for: the
+    // node list is bounded, and untracked senders are logged as "not in db and
+    // no need to insert". Everything below indexes nodes[] and dereferences the
+    // result, and nodes is an unordered_map - so operator[] would insert a null
+    // panel and the very next line would write through it. That is the
+    // StoreProhibited panic seen on a busy mesh, roughly once a minute, always
+    // right after a burst of POSITION_APP packets.
+    auto panelEntry = nodes.find(nodeNum);
+    if (panelEntry == nodes.end() || panelEntry->second == nullptr) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     int32_t altU = abs(alt) < 10000 ? alt : 0;
     char units[3] = {};
     if (db.config.display.units == meshtastic_Config_DisplayConfig_DisplayUnits_METRIC) {
